WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.170
- [Host] I think dumplings are amazing

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:03.910
because everyone loves it.

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:07.140
If you say dumping, everyone's faces will light up.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.370
- Hi, I'm Daniel and I'm making mandu today.

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.440
Mandu is a Korean-style dumpling, it's similar...

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.273
It's the Korean version

00:00:13.273 --> 00:00:15.630
of what a lot of Americans know as pot stickers.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.850
You know, I'm not entirely sure why they do use tofu.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.080
I actually didn't realize

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.090
that most other cultures don't use tofu.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.450
As for why you have to extract the water, if you don't,

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:25.360
it will make the mandu too watery.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.460
I got the basic recipe from my mom.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.650
My mom actually eyeballs most of the spices and what not,

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:33.936
so I had to get more exact specifications online.

00:00:33.936 --> 00:00:36.300
It's pretty rare to make mandu these days

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.150
unless it's for Korean New Years,

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:40.475
and even then me and my mom haven't made it in a while.

00:00:40.475 --> 00:00:42.920
After finding out that I made it for this video,

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.527
she actually wants to restart the tradition

00:00:44.527 --> 00:00:46.293
of making it for New Years again.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.513
True story.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:52.293
I use egg and water because it helps the skin stick better.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:53.173
For some reason,

00:00:53.173 --> 00:00:55.880
when I just use water, it never seems to stick.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.810
I don't know what everyone else's secret is.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:59.210
It just doesn't work for me.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.690
Growing up Korean-American, especially 'cause I'm only half,

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.660
was definitely a little bit confusing,

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.010
but one of the easiest ways to connect with Korean culture

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.105
and with my mom was always through food.

00:01:10.105 --> 00:01:12.480
Making mandu is one of the more fun ways

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.690
to connect with my Korean heritage.

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:17.040
Food in general has always been one of the easiest ways

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.580
for me and my mom to connect,

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:19.950
which was very important for her

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.470
and ultimately very important for me

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.430
to help me understand my heritage

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:24.803
and where my mom came from.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:26.740
- Hi, my name is Lisa,

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:28.620
and today I'm going to be making guotie.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.793
Guotie are Chinese dumplings otherwise known as pot sticker.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.763
We're using Napa cabbage.

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:37.090
We sprinkle salt on top of it

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:39.050
to help draw some of the water out

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:41.950
because we don't want too much moisture in the dumplings

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:44.573
because then it will be soggy and it'll fall apart.

00:01:44.731 --> 00:01:48.509
I don't remember exactly the first time

00:01:48.509 --> 00:01:51.140
we had guotie at home.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:54.870
I just always remember whenever there was Chinese New Year

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:58.780
or a special occasion my mom would make the dumplings.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:02.110
I just always remember them being an exciting part

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:05.210
because whenever there was something fun happening,

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:06.170
there'd be dumplings.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:09.113
So, I would know that it would be an exciting time.

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:12.230
When I was a kid, some of my favorite times

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.940
were getting to spend time with my mom in the kitchen.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:18.130
And we didn't have a lot of money when we were growing up,

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:20.050
but we always had enough food,

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:22.670
no matter how little money we had.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:26.040
And I had a lot of allergies growing up as well,

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.130
and I would remember that my mom would make me special food.

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:32.640
So, to me, I will always remember food is love,

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:36.460
and if I can help cook and I can feed other people,

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.383
that's a way that I can show other people love.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.200
- Hi, I'm Sanjana, and today I'm making Nepali momo.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.571
Nepali momo is a kind of steamed dumpling

00:02:44.571 --> 00:02:47.440
that's essentially Nepali street food.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.440
So, I'm not from Nepal.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.720
I'm actually South Indian, but my best friend, Nikita,

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:56.880
is Nepali and this recipe is actually her mom's.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.200
So, the thing that really excites me about momo

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.540
is that the flavors in the filling

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:02.770
are super familiar to me.

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:04.080
I've grown up on Indian cooking.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.774
My mom uses a lot of turmeric and a lot of gara masala

00:03:06.774 --> 00:03:10.180
amongst other spices in a lot of her cooking,

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:13.450
so when I had momo that was packaged inside of this

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:15.420
really tiny type of dumpling,

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.296
it was really fun to be able to have that much flavor

00:03:18.296 --> 00:03:20.640
that was just bite-sized and poppable.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.180
It was just a little piece of home

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.033
inside this really tiny dumpling.

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:27.820
As opposed to soy sauce, Nepali momo use a chutney.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:28.986
It just tastes so delicious

00:03:28.986 --> 00:03:32.263
with the filling that's inside the momo.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:35.570
Momo are definitely finger food, so use your hands,

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:38.407
pick up a momo, dip it in the sauce, and enjoy 'em.

00:03:38.859 --> 00:03:40.063
- Hi, I'm Rie.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:43.453
I'm making Japaneze gyoza dumpling today.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:45.473
Gyoze is Japanese-style dumpling.

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.680
I got this recipe from my mom

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.850
and she eyeballs all of the ingredients,

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:52.163
which is a typical mom thing to do.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.703
She used a lot of Nira chives.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:56.870
I think that it's the secret for her gyoza.

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:59.400
Gyoza is one of the first dish

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.412
I learned how to cook from my mom.

00:04:01.412 --> 00:04:03.742
The memory I have of making gyoza

00:04:03.742 --> 00:04:06.311
is how fast my mom can fold them.

00:04:06.311 --> 00:04:09.873
I would make one and she already made five.

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:13.200
It's been a while since I've made a gyoza with my mom,

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:16.543
but I bet she still makes them faster than me.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.441
I usually pan fry gyoza.

00:04:18.441 --> 00:04:20.793
After you line the gyoza in a pan,

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:23.579
you will add water to steam them.

00:04:23.579 --> 00:04:26.750
I'm adding a tablespoon of flour into the water

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.320
so it will create extra crispy base.

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:32.593
We call this hane, which translate to wings.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:35.473
This style of gyoza is really popular in Japan.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:39.282
When I make gyoza, I usually end up making hundreds of them.

00:04:39.282 --> 00:04:41.070
If freeze, it's great.

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:42.653
It's great for meal prep.

00:04:42.745 --> 00:04:45.963
Every culture has their own version of dumplings.

00:04:46.374 --> 00:04:47.960
Cooking connects people

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.453
and has a strong attachment to memory.

00:04:50.479 --> 00:04:52.130
I hope after watching this,

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:54.620
it will bring back all the fun memories you had

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:56.563
with your family or friends,

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.857
or create new one with some dumplings.

00:04:58.857 --> 00:05:00.563
- [Andrew] Oh, yes.

00:05:01.465 --> 00:05:04.215
(relaxing music)

